{"1-6":{"people":[],"places":[],"words":[{"base":"H4639","lemma":"מַעֲשֶׂה","tr":"ma·a·seh","gloss":"deed: work","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":235},{"base":"H2587","lemma":"חַנּוּן","tr":"chan·nun","gloss":"gracious","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":13},{"base":"H7349","lemma":"רַחוּם","tr":"ra·chum","gloss":"compassionate","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":13},{"base":"H5475","lemma":"סוֹד","tr":"sod","gloss":"counsel","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":21},{"base":"H2964","lemma":"טֶ֫רֶף","tr":"te·reph","gloss":"prey","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":22},{"base":"H2143","lemma":"זֵ֫כֶר","tr":"ze·kher","gloss":"memorial","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":23},{"base":"H1935","lemma":"הוֹד","tr":"hod","gloss":"splendor","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":24},{"base":"H1926","lemma":"הָדָר","tr":"ha·dar","gloss":"glory","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":30},{"base":"H6467","lemma":"פֹּ֫עַל","tr":"po·al","gloss":"work","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":37},{"base":"H2656","lemma":"חֵ֫פֶץ","tr":"che·phets","gloss":"pleasure","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":39}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"PSA","chapter":104,"verse":24,"verseEnd":24,"votes":12,"source":"both","text":"How many are Your works, O LORD! In wisdom You have made them all; the earth is full of Your creatures.","from":2},{"book":"PSA","chapter":138,"verse":1,"verseEnd":1,"votes":11,"source":"both","text":"I give You thanks with all my heart; before the gods I sing Your praises.","from":1},{"book":"PRO","chapter":24,"verse":14,"verseEnd":14,"votes":10,"source":"both","text":"Know therefore that wisdom is sweet to your soul. If you find it, there is a future for you, and your hope will never be cut off.","from":2},{"book":"PSA","chapter":149,"verse":1,"verseEnd":1,"votes":9,"source":"both","text":"Hallelujah! Sing to the LORD a new song— His praise in the assembly of the godly.","from":1},{"book":"PSA","chapter":2,"verse":8,"verseEnd":8,"votes":8,"source":"both","text":"Ask Me, and I will make the nations Your inheritance, the ends of the earth Your possession.","from":6},{"book":"PSA","chapter":80,"verse":8,"verseEnd":8,"votes":8,"source":"both","text":"You uprooted a vine from Egypt; You drove out the nations and transplanted it.","from":6},{"book":"PSA","chapter":106,"verse":1,"verseEnd":1,"votes":8,"source":"both","text":"Hallelujah! Give thanks to the LORD, for He is good; His loving devotion endures forever.","from":1},{"book":"PSA","chapter":109,"verse":30,"verseEnd":30,"votes":8,"source":"both","text":"With my mouth I will thank the LORD profusely; I will praise Him in the presence of many.","from":1}],"notes":[],"groups":[]},"7-10":{"people":[],"places":[],"words":[{"base":"H5703","lemma":"עַד","tr":"ad","gloss":"perpetuity","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":48},{"base":"H0571","lemma":"אֱמֶת","tr":"e·met","gloss":"truth: faithful","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":127},{"base":"H5769","lemma":"עוֹלָם","tr":"o·lam","gloss":"forever: enduring","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":438},{"base":"H6304","lemma":"פְּדוּת","tr":"pe·dut","gloss":"redemption","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":4},{"base":"H7922","lemma":"שֵׂ֫כֶל","tr":"se·khel","gloss":"understanding","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":16},{"base":"H6490","lemma":"פִּקּוּד","tr":"piq·qud","gloss":"precept","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":24},{"base":"H3374","lemma":"יִרְאָה","tr":"yir·ah","gloss":"fear","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":45},{"base":"H5564","lemma":"סָמַךְ","tr":"sa·makh","gloss":"to support","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":48},{"base":"H7225","lemma":"רֵאשִׁית","tr":"re·shit","gloss":"first: beginning","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":51},{"base":"H8416","lemma":"תְּהִלָּה","tr":"te·hil·lah","gloss":"praise","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":57}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"PRO","chapter":1,"verse":7,"verseEnd":7,"votes":25,"source":"both","text":"The fear of the LORD is the beginning of knowledge, but fools despise wisdom and discipline.","from":10},{"book":"PRO","chapter":9,"verse":10,"verseEnd":10,"votes":23,"source":"both","text":"The fear of the LORD is the beginning of wisdom, and knowledge of the Holy One is understanding.","from":10},{"book":"JOB","chapter":28,"verse":28,"verseEnd":28,"votes":21,"source":"both","text":"And He said to man, ‘Behold, the fear of the Lord, that is wisdom, and to turn away from evil is understanding.’”","from":10},{"book":"ECC","chapter":12,"verse":13,"verseEnd":13,"votes":16,"source":"both","text":"When all has been heard, the conclusion of the matter is this: Fear God and keep His commandments, because this is the whole duty of man.","from":10},{"book":"PSA","chapter":99,"verse":3,"verseEnd":3,"votes":10,"source":"both","text":"Let them praise Your great and awesome name— He is holy!","from":9},{"book":"PSA","chapter":19,"verse":7,"verseEnd":7,"votes":9,"source":"both","text":"The Law of the LORD is perfect, reviving the soul; the testimony of the LORD is trustworthy, making wise the simple.","from":7},{"book":"LUK","chapter":1,"verse":49,"verseEnd":49,"votes":9,"source":"both","text":"For the Mighty One has done great things for me. Holy is His name.","from":9},{"book":"LUK","chapter":1,"verse":68,"verseEnd":68,"votes":9,"source":"both","text":"“Blessed be the Lord, the God of Israel, because He has visited and redeemed His people.","from":9}],"notes":[],"groups":[]}}